// One block of a message: its text, and the setting that decides it.
//
// The active blocks of a message concatenate back to the exact text sent, so a client can render them
// separately without showing the reader something the model never receives. An inactive block has no
// text: it marks a setting that is switched off, at the point where it would land if it were on.
//
// Everything identifying a block is a machine value, never display copy — what a block is called,
// and what turning a switched-off one on would do, is for the client to say in the language it is
// running in.
